### What the model is
Per `../../xla.py` (at `HuggingFaceTB/SmolLM3-3B/xla.py`), this is the **FIBO text encoder = stock `SmolLM3Model`** (SmolLM3-3B with the LM head discarded), producing `last_hidden_state`. It runs **tensor-parallel Megatron-1D over a (1, 4) mesh** (4× Blackhole), at `CONTEXT_LENGTH=4096` (the passing default; 24576 OOMs). Q/K/V + MLP gate/up are column-parallel; O + MLP down are row-parallel → all-gather/reduce-scatter collectives per layer.

### Files
- **`main.py`** — the codegen (39,685 lines, ~1 MB). The whole model.
- **`utils.py`** — hand-written helpers: `DeviceGetter` singleton (opens the (1,4) mesh + fabric config), `get_scalar_from_tensor`, `load_tensor` (load → to_layout → to_dtype → to_device), `create_global_semaphore`. Clean; likely not the refactor target.
- **`__init__.py`** — just a license header.
- **`run`** — bash launcher (sets env, `python3 main.py`, optional Tracy).
- **`ttir_cpu.py`, `ttnn.mlir`, `irs/`, `generated/`, `tensors/`** — reference/support artifacts. `tensors/` holds 330 `argN.tensorbin` weight+activation files. No `model_ttnn.py`.

### Structure & entry points of `main.py`
Bottom-up call chain:
- `main()` (39677) → `load_activations_for__main()` + `load_weights_for__main()` → `_main(activations, weights)`.
- **`load_activations_for__main()`** (36510) — loads 3 activation tensors (`arg217/219/220`: input_ids int32, attention stuff, bf16).
- **`load_weights_for__main()`** (36547) — loads all 330 weights from `./tensors/argN.tensorbin` into the global dict `_main_weights`, keyed by HF names like `model.layers.35.mlp.gate_proj.weight`.
- **`consteval__main(ce_cache, weights)`** (36185) — one-time const-eval: calls `main_const_eval_0..47` on weight subsets, caches results in `ce_cache__main`.
- **`_main(activations, weights)`** (20033) — **the forward function.** Runs consteval, then the full 36-layer transformer as one flat straight-line sequence of `ttnn.*` ops, returning `[ttnn_rms_norm_72]` (final norm).

### Where the `ttnn.*` ops live
The forward body (`_main`, lines 20033–36182, ~16k lines) is the op-dense region. Op counts across the file: matmul (252), reshape (240), typecast (185), permute (126), to_layout/to_device (110 each), multiply/add (~110), rms_norm (73), reduce_scatter/all_gather/logical_not (72 each), softmax/sum/eq (36 each), where (38), plus split_query_key_value_and_split_heads, embedding, rotary sin/cos, repeat_interleave. **1,912 `ttnn.deallocate` calls** — nearly every intermediate is explicitly freed.

### Auto-generated / messy characteristics (for later refactoring)
- **SSA-style flat naming**: every value is `ttnn_<op>_<N>` (e.g. `ttnn_reshape_239`, `ttnn_add_107`), globally counted, never reused — no loops, no layer abstraction. The 36 transformer layers are fully unrolled into repeated near-identical blocks.
